\section{Missing data}{

The EquityTool rule is that a respondent with \strong{any} missing or
out-of-range answer receives no score. Such rows get \code{NA} for both \code{score}
and \code{quintile}. Set \code{na_rule = "partial"} to instead sum the available items
-- this is \strong{not} the official method, makes scores non-comparable across
respondents, and should only be used for diagnostics.
